       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. An overdose at that level can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nTypical adult dosing for hypertension or angina is 5 mg once daily. It can be titrated to 10 mg once daily, and the starting dose is often 2.5 mg in frail patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n\nPossible explanations are a typo (5 mg or 5.0 mg) or a mix-up with another drug or unit.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you need a dose above the labeled maximum for a specific reason, that should go through pharmacy and the attending. I can't enter it based on a verbal or unverified approval."
